<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33807" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">părastătĭcus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραστατικός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
			pilasters</i>, <i>parastatic</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Fabr. p. 688</span></i>, n.
			100.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">părastătĭca</span></b> ,
			ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραστατική</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A square pillar</i> or <i>column</i>,
				<i>a pilaster</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">columnae atque parastaticae (al. parastatae),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					33, 3, 15, § 52</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 9, 9</span></i>; cf. Inscr. Labus Epigrafe
			Lat. Scop. ap. Egitto, p. 7.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">părastătĭ-cae</span></b> ,
				ārum, f., <i>two bones in the knee of a horse</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Veg. Vet. 4, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
